   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "customData": null,
   "text": "(each force of the pair, not the net force)\nif A pushes on B, B pushes back on A:\nsame line of action,\nsame size, opposite direction\ne.g. push off the pool wall: it pushes you away\nnote: the two forces act on two different\nbodies, so they do not cancel (unlike Law I)",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "(each force of the pair, not the net force)\nif A pushes on B, B pushes back on A:\nsame line of action,\nsame size, opposite direction\ne.g. push off the pool wall: it pushes you away\nnote: the two forces act on two different\nbodies, so they do not cancel (unlike Law I)",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.35
  },
